Extender KLC terrain/colormap RLE decoder FUN_0000_643c (+ the split fragments
FUN_0000_6481 / FUN_0000_6542) drops the buffered-reader FUN_0000_5fbe's RETURN
cursor at all 9 refill sites, and FUN_0000_5fbe itself returns garbage.

FUN_0000_5fbe (the extender FILEMGR buffered reader) compacts the unconsumed tail
to the buffer start and refills; BOTH asm exit branches converge at
    602b: mov esi,[0x5564]   ; esi = buffer START (after compact+refill)
    6031: ret
so it ALWAYS returns esi = DAT_0000_5564.  Ghidra emitted the non-error return as
`CONCAT31(in_register_00000009,param_3)` (garbage) -> fixed to `DAT_0000_5564`.

Every decoder refill is the idiom
    cmp esi,[0x5568]; jb skip; call 5fbe   (or `push cont; jmp 5fbe`)
    skip: <use esi as the read cursor>
i.e. when the cursor reaches the buffer end [0x5568], 5fbe refills and the cursor
is reset to [0x5564].  Ghidra dropped the return at every site (keeping the stale
end-of-buffer cursor -> off-buffer read -> the observed 643c OOB / hang), and at
the tail-jump sites (`push 0x651f/0x657b; jmp 5fbe`, which RESUME the loop, not
return) it mangled the resume into a `return`.  Fix: thread 5fbe's return into the
per-site cursor (piVar15/puVar16/puVar17 in 643c; pbVar13/pbVar12/pbVar11/pbVar10/
param_5 in 6481/6542) and drop the spurious `return` so the loop continues.  The
eax accumulator (param_1/puVar5) is preserved by 5fbe (push/pop eax..ebx) and is
left untouched -- only the ESI cursor is reloaded, exactly as the asm does.

asm ground truth (objdump re_out/fist_image.bin):
    5fbe reader   : 602b mov esi,[0x5564]; 6031 ret   (single logical return = esi)
    643c hdr      : 6468 call 5fbe -> 646d lods eax (magic "KLC1")   cursor=esi
    643c pal-copy : 65c8 cmp esi,[0x5568]; 65d0 call 5fbe; 65d5 movsd
    643c decode   : 65f9 cmp esi,[0x5568]; 6601 call 5fbe; 6606 <decode>
    6481 row-rle  : 6517 cmp esi,[0x5568]; jae 652b (push 651f;jmp 5fbe -> RESUME)
    6481 term     : 6553 cmp esi,[0x5568]; jb 6560; 655b call 5fbe
    6481 pal-copy : 6573 cmp esi,[0x5568]; jae 6535 (push 657b;jmp 5fbe -> RESUME)
Verified: D32.KLC (heightmap), C32.KLC (colormap) and 5.SKY all decode through
FUN_0000_643c (callers re_out/fist_ext.c FUN staging: TCB+0x7a/+0x8a/+0xaa).
Flat32-module host-pointer-cursor / dropped-return class; never exercised before
op-0x18 (KDV streams via direct reads, not this buffered reader).

